Implement the selected mechanism, no headless work (Aster owns it).
Kit LaunchPlan describes a private runtime: real codex app-server --listen unix://<owned overlay>/codex.sock; TUI --remote the same endpoint. The server receives the per-invocation hooks/MCP/role config. Normal CODEX_HOME, no credential copy or global config write.
A short owned /tmp/bboxy-cx-<ULID> symlink points to the existing 0700 overlay when its physical path exceeds Darwin sun_path. The socket remains inside the overlay. Kit/facade cleanup verifies that the alias targets the owned overlay before removing it.
Host protocol adds generic optional CompanionSpec and CompanionInfo, no harness names. Supervisor owns the extra service as a direct child/process group, including exit watch, shutdown and reap. One EXTRA persistent process per live Codex seat; no startup worker or runtime thread per seat. Non-Codex seats have none.
The actor starts both children immediately, returning the existing Spawned reply with both owned PIDs. The private harness-exec CLI calls the kit's bounded socket-ready/exec helper inside that seat's PTY, then replaces itself with the Codex TUI without changing PID. Neither actor nor Logic's serial RPC waits for service readiness. Exact retries and recovery inventory see the seat even while the socket starts. Failed readiness exits the PTY with a named cause; normal lifecycle stops/reaps its service. Running macOS service exits reuse the existing kqueue child watch.
Mux maps the neutral plan to the generic host descriptor. Binding retains the actual supervisor-owned runtime PID/start/endpoint; Logic reattach reconstructs it from SeatInfo. refresh_adapters uses only that selected endpoint, never a user-global locator.
Native ID/status checks stay. Unknown/notLoaded produces NativeUnknown without mutation, automatic retry or PTY fallback. Bootstrap stays unavailable until SessionStart rebinds the thread; test that initial phase explicitly.

Required evidence: deterministic private service start/failed readiness/cancel/exit/reap and responsive other-seat tests; kit bootstrap and unknown-no-mutation vectors; a real Codex delegated task -> orient/report/reply/ACK with NO ctl start nudge; SIGKILL Logic and verify the same private runtime remains; close/expiry and assert no orphan. Every app run uses a fresh throwaway app account (file custody or debug memory selector as explicitly admissible); no operator Keychain or desktop. Hook prompts use asserted ctl recipes, no human input. Strict workspace all-target clippy and clean normal ci-local (no UI/lab/renderer changes), self-service max-two-gate claim and prompt own-target cleanup.

